From 3a7008a4b3279e4cf5a46db0990ee953cc425139 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: benmandrew <benmandrew@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:59:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep labels and numbering intact in diff output

- Attach a label on its own line to the heading, display equation, raw
  block or function call before it, so it keeps labelling that element.
  Added equations keep the label inside the diff-added wrapper, right
  after the equation; added headings put it after the wrapper.
- Emit deleted blocks of a replaced region in document order, and pair
  replaced atomic blocks of the same sort (equation, raw block, call to
  the same function, #let of the same name) as Changed.
- Deleted display equations are set with numbering: none, deleted
  headings become unnumbered #heading(...) calls, and labels of deleted
  content are dropped, so numbers match the new document.
- Mark added, deleted and changed function calls and #let bindings with
  diff-added-mark / diff-deleted-mark / diff-changed-mark margin notes
  placed with place(). Deleted calls are kept only as comments.
- Add --no-preamble to leave out the markup definitions, and document
  the names an imported markup file must define.
- Test an empty old file.
